From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_TEST_DISCARD_SAVE=1 (test only): the game works on a copy of its save for the session, the save itself is not written to

For the test runner: it puts the save back after every run (13 s of each 2 min 29 s), because
the game saves by itself. With this switch (exact "1") the first open or create of one of the
user's saves (account or device save of the user space) copies its folder to
/test-discard<the same path> under the same root, and every open, create and size file of that
save goes to the copy for the rest of the session. The copy is thrown away and made anew at
the next start. The save the session started from is still there afterwards.

A copy, not dropped writes: the game reads back what it wrote in the same session (a save, then
the file select screen), and dropped writes would hand it the old bytes.

One warning line at the first open says which copy is in use and whether the copy was made
("EDEN_TEST_DISCARD_SAVE: this session's save is the copy ..."). If the copy fails the session
still stays off the real save; the game then sees a missing or incomplete save and the line says
THE COPY FAILED.

A TEST switch: never in a play env. Nothing the game saves in such a session is kept. Off
without it: SessionSavePath returns the path it was given.

